### Phase 1 — Foundation (v3.0.0-alpha)

**Derive Eq 236, 237. Implement ANS + Context Mixing.**

These two changes alone will transform the compressor from "adequate" to "competitive with zstd/brotli." The ANS coder replaces Huffman everywhere (all existing strategies benefit), and context mixing adds the most powerful general-purpose strategy. **Expected combined improvement: 25-50% better compression on typical files.**

### Phase 2 — Enhancement (v3.0.0-beta)

**Derive Eq 238, 239, 241, 247, 249. Implement LZ overhaul, SA-IS BWT, prediction.**

Modernize the LZ engine, replace the naive BWT, and add descriptor prediction. These are "do it right" improvements that close the gap with state-of-the-art on specific data types. **Expected additional improvement: 10-25% beyond Phase 1.**

### Phase 3 — Optimization (v3.0.0-rc)

**Derive Eq 240, 242, 243, 244, 245, 246, 248. Implement routing v2, JIT, wavelet, EXE.**

Optimize strategy selection, add Sovereign JIT speed, wavelet decomposition, and EXE compilation. These provide diminishing-but-meaningful ratio improvements plus massive speed gains. **Expected additional improvement: 5-15% ratio + 10-50× speed.**

